From 8805924ce62c72b9e3ae7a48818af7ec61c73ba6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:51:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] utils: an HDR video that goes out as SDR is headed so on a
 connector that says nothing

The heading of the overview page of the player information (HeadCode())
says what the display is told. On a connector without the property
HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA the signal is not known, and an HDR video was headed
with nothing ("What the TV is sent could not be read" in Check this
setup), even where Kodi knows why the display is not told that it is
HDR (hdrNotSent: no HDR property, no HDR in the EDID, ...), which the
sentence under the heading then says. Such a video goes out as SDR: it
is headed hdr_lost ("SDR: the TV is not told this video is HDR"), as on
a connector that says SDR. Where Kodi does not know why, the heading
stays empty and the sentence says that what the TV is sent could not be
read, as before.
---
 xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h b/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h
index 1de035f..06d0f14 100644
--- a/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h
+++ b/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h
@@ -227,6 +227,10 @@ inline std::string HeadCode(const SummaryInput& in)
   // the connector does not say what it is told: an SDR file is SDR whatever it says
   if (in.signal.empty() && in.source == "sdr")
     return "sdr";
+  // ... and an HDR file whose display Kodi knows it does not tell that it is HDR (hdrNotSent: no HDR
+  // property on the connector, no HDR in the EDID, ...) goes out as SDR all the same
+  if (in.signal.empty() && hdr && !in.hdrNotSent.empty())
+    return "hdr_lost";
   return "";
 }
 
